    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d117">

                <pb facs="0156" n="146" sameAs="frus:frus1945v03/pg146"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Austria)/6–1945</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the State-War-Navy Coordinating Committee
                        to the Secretary of State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-06-19">19 June 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Secretaries of War and the Navy and the Joint Chiefs of Staff concur in the
                    recommendations of General McNarney in the attached copy of his cable on the
                    subject of the Subdivision of Vienna and recommend <pb facs="0157" n="147"
                        xml:id="pg147"/> that it be used as a basis for negotiations in the European
                    Advisory Commission.<anchor n="71" xml:id="d117-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>For the State-War-Navy Coordinating Committee: <lb/>
                    <signed>H. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Freeman Matthews</hi>
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Acting Chairman</hi>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d117-a1.xml" xpointer="d117-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d117-f1" n="71" xml:id="d117-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram 4933, June 19, to London, informed Ambassador Winant that General
                    McNarney’s recommendations had received the concurrence of the State, War, and
                    Navy Departments, and the Joint Chiefs of Staff; Ambassador Winant was directed
                    to proceed with negotiations in the European Advisory Commission for a protocol
                    on zones of occupation on the basis of those recommendations (740.00119
                    EAC/6–1445)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
